      "audio": {
        "id": "subtitle-clock-beat-1"
      },
      "narration": "This saddle is the surface z equals x squared minus y squared. Slice through the origin along the x direction, then the perpendicular y direction. Both curves belong to the same surface. Look at their bends. Take a moment to compare which section opens upward and which opens downward. The x section opens upward; the y section opens downward! Starting at the origin, move along the positive axes. The x section rises with increasingly positive slope. The y section falls with increasingly negative slope. Both start with zero slope.",
